---
// Equivalents.astro - Fun and tangible real-world volume analogies
---

<div id="equivalents-section" class="w-full bg-white rounded-xl border border-hairline p-5 shadow-xs">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-3 pb-2 border-b border-hairline">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-md bg-primary/10 border border-primary/20 flex items-center justify-center text-primary shrink-0">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
          <path d="M12 3c-3 4-4.5 7-4.5 9s1.5 5 4.5 9"></path>
          <path d="M12 3c3 4 4.5 7 4.5 9s-1.5 5-4.5 9"></path>
          <line x1="3" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12"></line>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink tracking-tight">Real-World Volume Equivalents</h3>
    </div>
    <span class="text-[11px] px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline text-ink-muted">
      Everyday Scale
    </span>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs text-ink-muted mb-3">
    To help visualize this volume in everyday terms, here is what it roughly equals:
  </p>

  <div id="equivalents-cards-grid" class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2.5">
    <!-- Populated by client script -->
    <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline text-center flex flex-col items-center justify-center">
      <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-white border border-hairline flex items-center justify-center text-primary mb-2 shadow-xs">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <rect x="6" y="3" width="12" height="18" rx="3"></rect>
          <line x1="6" y1="7" x2="18" y2="7"></line>
          <line x1="6" y1="17" x2="18" y2="17"></line>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <span class="text-xs text-ink-muted block">Enter dimensions to see real-world analogies</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
